      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T01:18:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this can be defined by us and therefore we don\u0027t have to follow the C++ way of encoding true and false. For example, the existence of the ramdump property (regardless of its value) could mean that ramdump is enabled.\n\nI think the point from Pierre is that there must be only one way of enabling ramdump. (accepting both ramdump\u003d3 and ramdump\u003d1 doesn\u0027t seem right.) So I agree with what Pierre said.",
      "parentUuid": "5d7933ad_1197a36f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 149,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 21
      },
